notes: "The second wall was the interface. With PowerPoint or Google Slides, the agent works through the screen. To judge a page it takes a full screenshot and looks at the picture. That is a bad loop: slow, expensive, and impossible to diff. You can't ask which object moved, or check bounds, or test a revision. Visual review still matters — a person still has to look — but it cannot be the only channel. I wanted the page to have a structure the agent could address directly."
